      "summary": "Sale Price Display — Original & Sale Price UI Across All Surfaces",
      "description": "As a \nShopper, \n\n\nI want\n to see both the original RRP and the active sale price when a product is on sale, \n\n\nso that\n I can clearly understand the discount I am receiving.\nPer PRC-09, when a sale pricebook entry is active in SFCC, the PWA must render a \n\"Was / Now\"\n price treatment across: Homepage, PLP product tiles, PDP, cart, checkout, wishlist, recommended product tiles, and order history.\nCross-epic dependency: PLP, PDP, Cart, Order History epics.\n\n\nDesign pattern:\n\"Was [RRP]\"\n — displayed in muted/grey styling. Always the base RRP pricebook price, regardless of any previous sale price.\n\"Now [sale price]\"\n — displayed in prominent green styling. Always the most recent active sale pricebook price.\n\"Was\" is always the base RRP — it does not reflect a previous promotional price or a prior sale price. \"Now\" is always the currently active sale pricebook entry.\n\n\nReference Image (Figma is leading)",
