      "id": "18827",
      "key": "SFCC-463",
      "summary": "Price Display Consistency — PWA Rendering Across All Surfaces",
      "description": "As a\n Shopper, \n\n\nI want\n to see prices displayed consistently in my local currency across every surface of the site, \n\n\nso that \nI always see the correct price regardless of where I am browsing.\nThe PWA must render the correct price consistently across: PLP, PDP, cart, wishlist, recommended product tiles, order history, recently viewed and checkout. The price source is either the SFCC pricebook for that storefront and currency, or — where no SFCC pricebook exists for the shopper's currency — the Global-e converted price derived from the base pricebook.\nThis is a PWA Kit frontend story. Currency display formatting rules (symbol, decimal places, separators) are configured in BM per \nhttps://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-46\n. \n\n\nCountry-to-currency mapping is configured per \nhttps://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-44\n. This story ensures the PWA applies those rules consistently across all surfaces.\nReference Image (Figma is leading)",
