      "id": "17882",
      "key": "SFCC-46",
      "summary": "Currency Display Formatting",
      "description": "As a\n Site Admin, \n\n\nI want \nto configure currency display formatting rules per currency in SFCC Business Manager, \n\n\nso that \nprices are displayed consistently and correctly formatted for each market's conventions.\nCurrency display formatting covers four elements per currency:\nSymbol\n — the currency symbol and its position (before amount, e.g. “$100\")\nDecimal places\n — number of decimal places displayed (e.g. 2 for AUD/GBP/EUR; 0 for zero-decimal currencies such as JPY, KRW, VND, IDR)\nDecimal separator\n — character separating integer and decimal portions (e.g. \".\" or \",\")\nThousands separator\n — character separating digit groups (e.g. \",\" or \".\")\nPRC-47 also requires correct minus-sign placement for refunds and credits per currency.\nNote: The rendering of formatted prices on the storefront (PLP, PDP, cart, checkout) is a PWA concern and is deferred to the relevant frontend epics.",
