    "value": "# Given a shopper navigates to a category page on desktop, when the page loads, then products are displayed in a 4-column grid.\n# Given a shopper navigates to a category page on tablet, when the page loads, then products are displayed in a 3-column grid.\n# Given a shopper navigates to a category page on mobile, when the page loads, then products are displayed in a 2-column grid.\n# Given a category page loads, when the initial product set is rendered, then up to 36 grid positions are filled — where editorial slots (e.g. hero cards) occupy grid positions, the number of product cards shown is reduced accordingly so the total grid positions displayed does not exceed 36.\n# Given a category has more than the initial page of results, when the page loads, then a \"View More\" button is displayed below the grid.\n# Given a shopper clicks \"View More\", then the next set of products appends to the existing grid without a full page reload.\n# Given all products have loaded, when the shopper clicks \"View More\" for the last time, then no further \"View More\" button is displayed."
