{
  "id": "18064",
  "key": "SFCC-80",
  "summary": "PLP UI - Product Grid Structure",
  "description": "**As a** Shopper, \n\n**I want** to browse a product listing page that clearly shows all products in a category as a grid of tiles, \n\n**so that** I can quickly scan, compare, and select products to explore further or add to my bag.\n\n----\n\nReference image (Figma is leading):\n\n![\"image-20260721-002221.png\"](image-20260721-002221.png)\n\n\n\n\n\nThis story covers the rendering of the product grid. \n\nThe individual product tile component is covered in [SFCC-236](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-236). \n\nThe product group grid component is covered in [SFCC-743](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-743) .\n\nThe PLP grid itself is not a component - but there is guidance on how this grid should be configured on figma here: \n\n[https://www.figma.com/design/wPiWmZZOVKnrENUWk2XWWm/Zimmermann*Design*System*2026?node-id=40000730-13635](https://www.figma.com/design/wPiWmZZOVKnrENUWk2XWWm/Zimmermann*Design*System*2026?node-id=40000730-13635)\n\n\n\nThe Contentful integration for editorial imagery embedded within the grid will be a separate user story and is not required to unblock this build.\n\n**Grid layout:**\n\n- 4-column grid on desktop; 3-column on tablet; 2-column on mobile.\n- Default number of products before \"View More\" is displayed is currently 36 singular standard product cards, but this should be adjustable. Also, the number of products shown is influenced by the inline editorial pieces. For example: in case there are 2 hero cards configured which take up 8 product card positions - then the number of products displayed would be 28 products given the hero cards are also products.\n- \"View More\" pattern loads additional products on click without a full page reload.",
